---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2>Anchor. Seal. Check.</h2>
    <p class="lead">No model in the loop: DocKeeper compares normalized code blocks by fingerprint. The result is the same every time you run it.</p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">01</span>
        <h3>Anchor every claim</h3>
        <p>Next to each sentence, point at the code that proves it: by symbol, by line, hidden in a comment, or stored outside the text.</p>
        <div class="snip">&#91;&#91;src/payments.py#validate_payment&#93;&#93;</div>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/markdown.py#analizar -->
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">02</span>
        <h3>It becomes a block</h3>
        <p>The whole enclosing function, class or method, not a fragile line range. Outside definitions, a small window around the line.</p>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/bloques.py#bloque_en -->
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">03</span>
        <h3>Seal a fingerprint</h3>
        <p>Normalized and hashed: reformatting is harmless, logic changes are not. The seal file stores hashes, never code.</p>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/huellas.py#normalizar_linea dockeeper/sello.py#Entrada -->
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">04</span>
        <h3>Check, anytime</h3>
        <p>Locally, in a git hook or on every pull request. The exit code tells CI whether your docs are still true.</p>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/motor.py#verificar_codigo -->
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="verdicts">
      <div class="verdict v-ok"><b>OK</b> <span class="exit">exit 0</span><p>Same block, same place. Nothing to do.</p></div>
      <div class="verdict v-mv"><b>MOVED</b> <span class="exit">exit 0</span><p>Same block, elsewhere in the file. <code>dockeeper fix</code> relocates it for you.</p></div>
      <div class="verdict v-ch"><b>CHANGED</b> <span class="exit">exit 1</span><p>The code changed. A person rewrites the claim, then accepts the new block.</p></div>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <div class="scroll"><img src={`${base}assets/how-it-works.svg`} alt="Diagram: a claim in docs/payments.md is anchored to the whole validate_payment function, the block is normalized and hashed into the seal file, and check reports OK, MOVED or CHANGED" width="960" height="330" loading="lazy"></div>
      <figcaption>The same example end to end. <code>fix</code> only ever touches the seal file: it never rewrites your documents.</figcaption>
      <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/motor.py#arreglar -->
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
